Syria imposes curfew in Ayn al-Arab after attacks on government facilities 






                  Syrian authorities imposed a temporary curfew in Ayn al-Arab following attacks against government buildings, according to state media. 

 Citing a security source, Alikhbaria TV said a group of people launched assaults against government facilities, with&nbsp;Internal security forces reinforcing their presence across the area to impose order and pursue suspects.&nbsp;

